2500013 (R2-2411244)], RAN1 has reached the further agreement regarding question 2a and 2b: Regarding the issue on differentiation of sTRP and sDCI mTRP, we provide our views in this contribution. 2 Discussion As discussed in our previous contributions [R1-2501830], for simultaneous unified TCI state(s) update for a list of cells, what to be differentiated are: sTRP in Rel-17 UTCI framework and sDCI mTRP in Rel-18 eUTCI framework. Among two alternatives, we prefer Alt2 due to following reasons: The essential difference between sTRP and sDCI based mTRP is the number of indicated TCI states, which is determined by which kind of TCI state MAC CE command, among Unified TCI States Activation/Deactivation MAC CE (TS 38.321 clause 6.1.3.47), Enhanced Unified TCI States Activation/Deactivation MAC CE for Joint TCI States (TS 38.321 clause 6.1.3.70), or Enhanced Unified TCI States Activation/Deactivation MAC CE for Separate TCI States (TS 38.321 clause 6.1.3.71), is received. When a UE receives any above TCI state activation MAC CE command, the TCI states are activated for all CCs/DL BWPs in simultaneousU-TCI-UpdateListX if configured, which guarantees all CCs in the list will be indicated with same number of TCI states. Given the following conclusion drawn in RAN1#115, UE does not expect to receive Unified TCI States Activation/Deactivation MAC CE after receiving Enhanced Unified TCI States Activation/Deactivation MAC CE for Joint TCI States, or Enhanced Unified TCI States Activation/Deactivation MAC CE for Separate TCI States. In other words, once a UE operates as sDCI mTRP in a set of CCs/BWPs, it will never operate as sTRP anymore. Therefore, there is no need to differentiate the cells operated as sTRP or sDCI mTRP by any RRC parameters as given in Alt1 because the current spec has guaranteed all CCs in the list operate in the same mode. However, current field description is incomplete without capturing the two MAC CEs for s-DCI based mTRP introduced in Rel-18. We propose to update the field description as follows: 3 Recommended reply to the LS With the above understanding, kindly please find the replies on the second issue below: 2. sTRP vs sDCI mTRP Question 2a: RAN2 would like to ask if RAN1 has any concern on the above highlight sentence? Answer 2a: Yes. There is no need to differentiate the cells operated as sTRP or sDCI mTRP by any RRC parameters because the current spec has guaranteed all CCs in the list should operate in the same mode. The essential difference between sTRP and sDCI based mTRP is the number of indicated TCI states, which is determined by which kind of TCI state MAC CE command, among Unified TCI States Activation/Deactivation MAC CE (TS 38.321 clause 6.1.3.47), Enhanced Unified TCI States Activation/Deactivation MAC CE for Joint TCI States (TS 38.321 clause 6.1.3.70), or Enhanced Unified TCI States Activation/Deactivation MAC CE for Separate TCI States (TS 38.321 clause 6.1.3.71), is received. When a UE receives any above TCI state activation MAC CE command, the TCI states are activated for all CCs/DL BWPs in simultaneousU-TCI-UpdateListX if configured, which guarantees all CCs in the list will be indicated with same number of TCI states. The sentence highlighted in yellow is not proper to differentiate sDCI based mTRP and sTRP. Moreover, the field description does not capture TCI state activation/deactivation by the Enhanced Unified TCI States Activation/Deactivation MAC CE for Joint TCI States as specified in TS 38.321 clause 6.1.3.70, or Enhanced Unified TCI States Activation/Deactivation MAC CE for Separate TCI States as specified in TS 38.321 clause 6.1.3.71 for sDCI mTRP in Rel-18 eUTCI. Question 2b: If there is any concern on Question 2a, what’s RAN1’s suggestion on how to sepa

